      "title": "The Administration and the Commissioner",
      "narration": "The Maryland Insurance Administration is the state agency that regulates insurance, headed by the Insurance Commissioner, who is appointed by the Governor. The Commissioner enforces the Insurance Article and the regulations adopted under it. The Administration licenses producers and insurers, examines insurers for solvency, reviews and approves policy forms and rates, investigates consumer complaints, holds hearings, issues orders and penalties and publishes regulations and bulletins. Theo will deal with the Administration as a licensee, as the person complaints about him are sent to, and as the regulator whose rulings decide what his insurers may sell.",
