      "title": "Voluntary deposits are not commingling",
      "text": "A producer may deposit its own funds into the premium account to cover shortfalls or bank charges, and may hold several carriers’ premiums together, without violating the commingling rule. What is prohibited is mixing premium funds into an operating or personal account or drawing the premium account below the amounts owed.",
